From 881a25477bb087a5dd81a8a5b478acff6f7dfdc5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adrien Delmas <adrien@adriendelmas.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 16:49:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 25/57] kernel/scene: MaterialX-exact procedural noise nodes

Imported from Blender PR #158054 (materialx-noise-nodes), Cycles side only -
the Blender node, RNA and EEVEE parts are left out, as is blender/shader.cpp
which standalone Cycles does not have. Blender's own Noise, Voronoi and White
Noise do not share MaterialX's hash functions, normalisation constants or
parameter semantics, so a MaterialX graph remapped onto them never matches the
reference; these nodes are an exact target instead.

Two changes against the original: compile_begin takes the owning node in this
branch, and the Vector input now falls back to texture coordinates the way the
other procedural textures do rather than evaluating everywhere at the origin.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
